# V90Phase3Demodulator: the V.90 / V.92 phase-3 (RX) state machine (the demodulator side of the line probing: Sd / SdNot / TRN1d / Jd / DIL / QTS / ANSpcm), 0x42c bytes on i386, a plain class (no vptr); V90Demodulator embeds it.
# It EMBEDS a V90Phase3Modulator (+0x34, the probing signal it knows: the P27 class, flattened here as mod_*; the demodulator reads its event_ / segCnt_ / isRef_ / code_), a
# SerialDifferentialDecoder<int> (+0x3cc) and a Descrambler<int,int> (+0x3d0, flattened as descr_*); the V90SdDetector (0x1c B) and the ANSamToneDetector (0x3c B) are heap objects it allocates in the constructor.
# The objects it USES (V90AutoDigitalImpDetector, V90Parameters, V90Jd, V92Jd, tagV90DILdescriptor) are plain pointers.  Member names are descriptive (the vendor's are unknown); the states come from the debug strings.
class V90Phase3Demodulator size 0x42c cxx P34_V90Phase3Demodulator mirror Ph3DemObj
